{
 "name": "crystal_palace_iguanodons",
 "description": "The two Victorian Crystal Palace Iguanodon statues (Benjamin Waterhouse Hawkins, 1854) on their grassy island, drawn as painted sculptures: LEFT a heavy rhino-like standing quadruped facing right with pillar legs, painted green-grey #6f8a5a with scale strokes and pale sheen highlights, nose horn at about (-260,-320); RIGHT a half-reclining one facing left, propped on a straight front leg with its tail curled along the plinth, nose horn at about (+318,-305). Both on low grey stone plinths; grass island with earth bank, stones, tufts and a fern clump in the middle. Anchor bottom-centre, x -500..500, y -365..0 (open grass in the middle around x -200..240 for Doug).",
